{
  "_comment": [
    "Classification of every \"palette.*\" string literal in the app sources, checked by",
    "the palette agent surface guard script. A new palette command fails that guard",
    "until it is classified here, so publishing a command to agents through",
    "`cmux palette list` stays a decision instead of a side effect.",
    "dynamicFamilies also covers ids built by interpolation: the guard reads the static",
    "prefix in front of each `\\(` and fails until this file declares that family.",
    "excludedCommandIds must match CommandPaletteAgentSurface.notAgentSurfaceCommandIds.",
    "probeBackedContextKeys names the context keys an availability probe answers, which",
    "read false until the probe runs. The guard rejects them inside any contribution's",
    "`when` argument, and inside any predicate named `...Enablement` passed to `when`,",
    "because in the agent listing a false `when` removes the row while a false",
    "`enablement` keeps it and reports isEnabled false. Each name must also carry the",
    "`Probe-backed:` marker in its doc comment in CommandPaletteContextKeys.swift."
  ],
